text:
That color of rose and lily, that delightful, sweet, honest gaze, that lovely white upright neck, and ruby mouth filled with pearls;


the alabaster hand that binds the one most set against love and banishes and estranges the freest, most tyrannical resolve from souls;


that rich and lovely spring, whose flowers of grace and beauty angry time cannot offend:


these cause me to live and die, and are the beginning, end, and relief of my care, my rest, and my happiness.
